[I] Daemon for managing internet connections

[T] ConnMan (Connection Manager) is a lightweight daemon for managing
[T] internet connections on embedded and desktop Linux systems. It supports
[T] Ethernet, WiFi, Bluetooth and cellular via plugins and provides DHCP,
[T] IPv6, DNS proxy, WISPr hotspot login and a D-Bus API.

[U] https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/network/connman/connman.git

